    <item>
      <title>Getting Started with TI CC2650 LaunchPad and Contiki</title>
      <link>http://pablocorbalan.com/post/getting-started-with-ti-cc2650-launchpad/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 May 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://pablocorbalan.com/post/getting-started-with-ti-cc2650-launchpad/</guid>
      <description>I just bought two TI CC2650 LaunchPads from Mouser, which feature the recently released TI CC2650 System-on-a-Chip (SoC), and I thought I could write a simple tutorial to help people get started with the LaunchPad and Contiki OS on Mac OS X.
The CC2650 SoC integrates an ARM Cortex-M3 microcontroller together with a Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) and IEEE 802.15.4 radio chip. This SoC brings new opportunities for wireless devices and research.</description>
    </item>
    
